final details revealed today in the  death of the man who killed trooper  micah may during a pursuit on i-15 last  july a fact-finding review held this  morning regarding 60-year-old douglas  claiborne as joe moeller reports it was  explained why law enforcement had no  choice but to shoot him during the  confrontation  the person was described as being  distraught and holding a butcher style  knife in their hand investigators say it  all started with a carjacking they broke  down why douglas claiborne was shot and  killed the decedent did not stop for the  troopers and they initiated vehicle  pursuit the pursuit went on for 42  minutes this is video from metro's  helicopter  it shows the moment trooper micah may  was hit and when troopers did a pit  maneuver before opening fire this is  from a patrol car it shows trooper may  running right before he got hit trooper  micah may attempted to set up stop  sticks on i-15 southbound investigators  say four law enforcement officers opened  fire on claiborne the officers during  their statements  two of them commented specifically that  they could see the suspect grabbing for  trooper may's weapon a toxicology report  revealed a large amount of meth in  claiborne's system in this particular  instance the decedent's levels of  methamphetamine being 9 000 nanograms  per milliliter it's fair to say that's  extremely high that's extremely high may  died two days later after being hit  investigators say they don't know if  claiborne intentionally hit may or not  the hearing ended with written public  questions did the trooper who was struck  by the suspect violates safety protocol  by crossing multiple lanes of traffic  exposing himself from a protected  position in order to deploy stop sticks  i can't speak to nhp's training or  policies on what or would not be  considered violation of safety protocols  joe muller live local now
 

